{
 "template": "motion_transfer",
 "version": 1,
 "task": "motion_transfer",
 "description": "Make the person in a still photo perform the motion of a driving video, keeping the driving video's scene. WAN 2.1 VACE 1.3B. The control video is an animated WEBP uploaded through the normal image endpoint - core LoadImage concatenates every frame of an animated file into one IMAGE batch, which is why no video-loading node pack is needed. control_masks decide what is rebuilt: 1 = regenerate (the person), 0 = keep the driving pixels exactly (the background). reference_image is NOT frame 0 of the output - VACE encodes it and prepends it as one extra latent frame that the model attends to, then TrimVideoLatent slices it off; it carries appearance, not composition. length MUST be 4n+1 (17/21/25/29/33). Measured ceiling on 8 GB VRAM / 16 GB RAM: 480x480 x 25 frames is comfortable at ~4.5 min; 480x832 x 33 peaked at 7.99 of 8.00 GB and must not be exceeded.",
 "required_models": [
  "wan21-vace-1.3b",
  "wan21-vae",
  "wan-umt5-xxl"
 ],
